:isQuietRoute a owl:DatatypeProperty,
        owl:FunctionalProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Belonging to a quieter route"@en ;
    :XMLName "IHS_QuietRoute" ;
    :applicable "Y" ;
    :formatNote "in XML: Y/N" ;
    :legalDeadline "1 January 2021"@en ;
    :rinfIndex "1.1.1.1.7.11" ;
    :shaclShapeValidationRule <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/IsQuietRoute> ;
    dcterms:created "2020-11-04"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:modified "2024-01-08"^^xsd:date,
        "2025-02-28"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:comment "Belonging to a 'quieter route' in accordance with Article 5b of TSI NOI."@en ;
    rdfs:domain [ ],
        [ ],
        [ ] ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy : ;
    rdfs:range xsd:boolean ;
    rdfs:seeAlso "Art 5b of Regulation (EU) 1304/2014 (amended by Regulation (EU) 2019/774) of 16 May 2019" ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf :healthSafetyAndEnvironmentDataParameter ;
    ns1:term_status "stable" ;
    skos:scopeNote """Art 5B: A quieter route means a part of the railway infrastructure with a minimum length of 20 km on which the average number of daily operated freight trains during the night-time as defined in national legislation transposing Directive 2002/49/EC of the European Parliament and of the Council (5) was higher than 12. The freight traffic in the years 2015, 2016 and 2017 shall be the basis for the calculation of that average number. In case the freight traffic due to exceptional circumstances diverges in a given year from that average number by more than 25 %, the Member State concerned can calculate the average number on the basis of the remaining two years.
Art 5.C 1:   Member States shall designate quieter routes in accordance with Article 5b and the procedure set out in Appendix D.1 of the Annex. They shall provide the European Union Agency for Railways ( the Agency ) with a list of quieter routes six months after the date of publication of this Regulation at the latest. The Agency shall publish those lists on its website."""@en .

:localRulesOrRestrictions a owl:DatatypeProperty,
        owl:FunctionalProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Existence of rules and restrictions of a strictly local nature"@en ;
    :XMLName "RUL_LocalRulesOrRestrictions" ;
    :applicable "Y/N" ;
    :formatNote "Y/N" ;
    :legalDeadline "1 January 2021"@en ;
    :rinfIndex "1.1.1.4.1",
        "1.2.3.1" ;
    :shaclShapeValidationRule <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/LocalRulesOrRestrictions> ;
    dcterms:created "2021-08-09"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:modified "2021-09-12"^^xsd:date,
        "2025-03-11"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:comment "Existence of rules and restrictions of a strictly local nature"@en ;
    rdfs:domain [ ],
        [ ],
        [ ] ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy : ;
    rdfs:range xsd:boolean ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf :rulesDataParameter ;
    ns1:term_status "stable" ;
    skos:scopeNote """There is a general obligation for Member States to notify existing national rules but:  Member States may decide not to notify rules and restrictions of a strictly local nature. In such cases, Member States shall mention those rules and restrictions in the registers of infrastructure.
In this eventuality, this parameter allows the IM accordingly to its Member State decision to declare the existence of such rules and to provide them with the parameter 'Documents regarding the rules or restrictions of a strictly local nature available by the IM'"""@en .

