:trackPhaseInfo a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Information on phase separation"@en ;
    :XMLName "EOS_InfoPhase" ;
    :applicable "Y/N" ;
    :dependencyNote "A value is mandatory only if 1.1.1.2.4.1.1 parameter \"Phase separation\" value is \"Y\" (true), otherwise applicability flag is \"N\" (not applicable)"@en ;
    :formatNote """In RDF the range is an instance of the era:PhaseInfo class with all its properties.

For RINF XML data sets:
As long as the data provision through XML data sets is allowed, the data format is a character string with the following structure: distance type [MIN/MAX] + length [NNN] + switch off breaker [Y/N] + lower pantograph [Y/N] + km [NNN.NNN]. The structure of the string is as follows:
- distance type [MIN/MAX] - single selection of 'MIN=minimum' or 'MAX=maximum' to show whether the length is a minimum distance between the inner contact strips of the pantographs or a maximum distance between the outer contact strips of the pantographs. Multiple strings for this parameter are accepted;
- length [NNN] - the length of the phase separation in meters;
- switch off breaker [Y/N], single selection of 'yes' or 'no' to show whether the breaker has to be switched off;
- lower pantograph [Y/N], single selection of 'yes' or 'no' to show whether the pantograph has to be lowered,
- Km [NNN.NNN] - the location from the start of the line where the new value is valid."""@en ;
    :legalDeadline "In accordance with Implementing Decision 2014/880/EU and by 16 March 2019 at the latest"@en ;
    :rinfIndex "1.1.1.2.4.1.2" ;
    :shaclShapeValidationRule <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/TrackPhaseInfo>,
        <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/TrackPhaseInfoApplicability> ;
    dcterms:created "2023-04-05"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:modified "2025-02-18"^^xsd:date,
        "2025-02-28"^^xsd:date,
        "2025-06-09"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:replaces :phaseInfo ;
    rdfs:comment "Relates the Track with PhaseInfo. Indication of required several information on phase separation."@en ;
    rdfs:domain [ ],
        [ ],
        [ ] ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy : ;
    rdfs:range :PhaseInfo ;
    rdfs:seeAlso "ENE TSI: 4.2.15" ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf :oclSeparationSectionsObjParameter ;
    ns1:term_status "stable" .

:trackSystemSeparationInfo a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Information on system separation"@en ;
    :XMLName "EOS_InfoSystem" ;
    :applicable "Y/N" ;
    :dependencyNote "Mandatory if there is an indication of existence of system separation (parameter 1.1.1.2.4.2.1)"@en ;
    :formatNote """In RDF, the range is an instance of the era:SystemSeparationInfo class with all its properties.

For RINF XML data sets:
As long as the data provision through XML data sets is allowed, the data format is a character string with the following structure: length [NNN] + switch off breaker [Y/N] + lower pantograph [Y/N] + km [NNN.NNN] """ ;
    :legalDeadline "In accordance with Implementing Decision 2014/880/EU and by 16 March 2019 at the latest"@en ;
    :rinfIndex "1.1.1.2.4.2.2" ;
    :shaclShapeValidationRule <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/TrackSystemSeparationInfo>,
        <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/TrackSystemSeparationInfoApplicability> ;
    dcterms:created "2023-04-05"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:modified "2025-02-18"^^xsd:date,
        "2025-02-28"^^xsd:date,
        "2025-06-09"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:replaces :systemSeparationInfo ;
    rdfs:comment "Indication of required several information on system separation"@en ;
    rdfs:domain [ ],
        [ ],
        [ ] ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy : ;
    rdfs:range :SystemSeparationInfo ;
    rdfs:seeAlso "ENE TSI: 4.2.16" ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf :oclSeparationSectionsObjParameter ;
    ns1:term_status "stable" ;
    skos:scopeNote """Length - the length of the system separation in meters
Switch off breaker - single selection of  Y=yes  or  N=no  to show whether the breaker has to be switched off
Lower pantograph - single selection of  Y=yes  or  N=no  to show whether the pantograph has to be lowered
Km - the location from the start of the line where the new value is valid """@en .

:tsiMagneticFields a owl:DatatypeProperty,
        owl:FunctionalProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Existence and TSI compliance of rules for magnetic fields emitted by a vehicle"@en ;
    :applicable "Y/N/NYA" ;
    :dependencyNote "Applicable ( Y ) only when for parameter 1.1.1.3.7.1 the selected option is wheel detector. The parameter is not applicable when the rules do not exist."@en ;
    :formatNote "Y/N" ;
    :legalDeadline "12 months after publication of Article 7 Guide for OP tracks"@en,
        "In accordance with Implementing Decision 2014/880/EU and by 16 March 2019 at the latest"@en ;
    :rinfIndex "1.1.1.3.9.1",
        "1.2.1.1.8.1" ;
    :shaclShapeValidationRule <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/TsiMagneticFields>,
        <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/TsiMagneticFieldsApplicability> ;
    dcterms:created "2024-04-18"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:modified "2024-09-19"^^xsd:date,
        "2025-02-18"^^xsd:date,
        "2025-02-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:relation :trainDetectionSystemType ;
    dcterms:replaces :TSIMagneticFields ;
    dcterms:source <http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg_impl/2023/1695/oj> ;
    rdfs:comment "Indication whether rules exist and are compliant with the TSI."@en ;
    rdfs:domain [ ],
        [ ],
        [ ] ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy : ;
    rdfs:range xsd:boolean ;
    rdfs:seeAlso "https://www.era.europa.eu/system/files/2023-09/index077_-_ERA_ERTMS_033281_v5.pdf"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf :relatedElectromagneticInterferencesDataParameter ;
    ns1:term_status "stable" ;
    skos:scopeNote """The electromagnetic fields generated by rolling stock can interfere with the operation of axle counters and wheel detectors.
                      'True' means the rules exist and are compliant with the frequency management specified in the TSI.
                      'False' means the rules exist and are not compliant with the frequency management specified in the TSI.

                      Verification of compliance with TSI includes application of notified national rules (when they exist) in case of part covered by open point."""@en .

:tsiTractionHarmonics a owl:DatatypeProperty,
        owl:FunctionalProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Existence and TSI compliance of limits in harmonics in the traction current of vehicles"@en ;
    :applicable "Y/N/NYA" ;
    :legalDeadline "12 months after publication of Article 7 Guide for OP tracks"@en,
        "In accordance with Implementing Decision 2014/880/EU and by 16 March 2019 at the latest"@en ;
    :rinfIndex "1.1.1.3.9.2",
        "1.2.1.1.8.2" ;
    :shaclShapeValidationRule <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/TsiTractionHarmonics>,
        <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/TsiTractionHarmonicsApplicability> ;
    dcterms:created "2024-04-18"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:modified "2024-09-19"^^xsd:date,
        "2025-02-18"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:relation :trainDetectionSystemType ;
    dcterms:replaces :TSITractionHarmonics ;
    dcterms:source <http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg_impl/2023/1695/oj> ;
    rdfs:comment "Indication whether rules exist and are compliant with the TSI."@en ;
    rdfs:domain [ ],
        [ ],
        [ ] ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy : ;
    rdfs:range xsd:boolean ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf :relatedElectromagneticInterferencesDataParameter ;
    ns1:term_status "stable" ;
    skos:scopeNote """Compatibility with track circuits and wheel detectors of axle counters.

The harmonics in the traction current in the rails can interfere with the operation of track circuits. The DC current in the rails may saturate the detectors of the axle counters, preventing their operation.

'Y' means the rules exist and are compliant with the frequency management specified in the TSI.
'N' 'means the rules exist and are not compliant with the frequency management specified in the TSI.

Verification of compliance with TSI includes application of notified national rules (when they exist) in case of part covered by open point.
LOC&PAS TSI : Appendix J-2, index 1, clause 3.2.2"""@en .

